d Excel, demonstrating skills in scripting, problem-solving, and stakeholder interaction. Collaborated with key stakeholders to enhance project deliverables and satisfaction\n[1]Skills: Programming Languages: Technical Skills: Scripting, Data Entry, Python; Soft Skills: Communication, Problem Solving, Stakeholder Interaction\n[1]Job Title: Freelance 3D Designer\n[1]Company: Freelance\n[1]Location: Toronto, ON, Canada\n[1]Duration: 2024/01 - 2024/09\n[1]Description: Designed quality models for 3D printed products, utilizing Blender and various slicing and printing software/hardware. Proficient in 3D modeling and product design\n[1]Skills: Programming Languages: ; Technical Skills: Python, 3D Printing, Blender, Product Design, 3D Modelling; Soft Skills: Good Written and Communication Skills, Fast Learning\n[1]Job Title: Secretary and Sales Associate\n[1]Company: Medica Providencia Clinic\n[1]Location: Tuxtla Gtz, CS, Mexico\n[1]Duration: 2015/08 - 2018/07\n[1]Description: Efficiently managed secretarial tasks during peak hours, showcasing time management skills. Demonstrated customer service and adaptability in sales operations at pharmacy and store sections\n[1]Skills: Programming Languages: ; Technical Skills: Data Entry, Microsoft Suite; Soft Skills: Time Management, Customer Service, Adaptability\n[0]Projects:\n[1]Project Title: Horizontal Federated Learning Research\n[1]URL: github.com/alexjsenn/FedScale\n[1]Type: Research | Capstone Project\n[1]Duration: 2021/09 - 2022/06\n[1]Description: Developed algorithm that doubled network efficiency with comparable model performance, utilizing C++/Python. Co-authored technical papers and presentations on novel aggregation algorithms\n[1]Skills: Programming Languages: Technical Skills: C++, Python, Unit Testing, Distributed Systems; Soft Skills: Good Written and Communication Skills, Teamwork\n[1]Project Title: MAPPA C++ Geographical Information System\n[1]URL: https://github.com/Marneus981/MAPPA\n[1]Type: University Project\n[1]Duration: 2019/09 - 2020/06\n[1]Description: Built a GIS system using OpenStreetMap data and C++ EZGL Library, improving algorithm efficiency by 200% and reducing memory usage by 50%. Co-developed UI/UX tailored to stakeholder needs\n[1]Skills: Programming Languages: C++; Technical Skills: Algorithm Optimization, OpenStreetMap API; Soft Skills: Teamwork\n[1]Project Title: Neural Signal Modelling\n[1]URL: https://github.com/Marneus981/NeuralBioelectricityProject\n[1]Type: University Project\n[1]Duration: 2020/09 - 2020/12\n[1]Description: Coalesced research on neural signal transmission and propagation using MATLAB, showcasing analytical problem-solving skills. Demonstrated ability to simulate complex systems\n[1]Skills: Programming Languages: MATLAB; Technical Skills: Data Analysis, Neuroscience, Machine Learning; Soft Skills: Detail-Oriented, Research\n[1]Project Title: TTRPG Tools\n[1]URL: https://github.com/Marneus981/TTRPGTools\n[1]Type: Open Source Personal Project\n[1]Duration: 2023/06 - Present\n[1]Description: Implemented automated debugging and scripting for a set of software tools, leveraging AI integration to enhance TTRPG game development. Utilized C++/Python programming languages to develop software components\n[1]Skills: Programming Languages: C++, Python; Technical Skills: Version Control with Git, Automated Testing, Scripting, Software Development Cycle, Debugging; Soft Skills: Proactiveness, Multitasking, Fast Learning\n[1]Project Title: Magia Chef\n[1]URL: \n[1]Type: Personal Game Project\n[1]Duration: 2023/06 - Present\n[1]Description: Developed a 3D roguelike shooter video game using Unity, showcasing C# programming skills and 3D asset creation. Utilized Blender for modeling and Unity's built-in toolset for animation\n[1]Skills: Programming Languages: C#; Technical Skills: Back-End Development, Unity 3D, 3D Animation, AI Coding Tools; Soft Skills: Proactiveness", 'job_description': "**Company Name:** Sentry\n**Job Title:** Software Engineer, New Grad\n\n**Key Responsibilities:**\n\n1. Develop and extend the Sentry product by writing software in either Python or JavaScript (or both)\n2. Participate in the full software development lifecycle - design, development, testing, and operating in production\n3. Communicate effectively with team members, other teams, and stakeholders\n4. Act on feedback, coaching, and mentorship from manager and teammates\n\n**Requirements:**\n\n1. B.S. or higher in Computer Science (or similar degree program)\n2. At least 1 previous internship or equivalent practical experience\n3. Implementation skills with one or more general-purpose programming languages (e.g., Python, JavaScript, Java, etc.)\n4. Good knowledge of algorithms, data structures, and object-oriented design principles\n5. Experience working with version control and unit testing\n\n**Needed Skills:**\n\n**Technical Skills:**\n\n1. Programming languages: Python, JavaScript, Java, etc.\n2. Version control: experience with a VCS (e.g., Git)\n3. Unit testing: familiarity with testing frameworks and practices\n4. Algorithms and data structures: understanding of fundamental concepts\n\n**Soft Skills:**\n\n1. Communication: ability to effectively collaborate with team members and stakeholders\n2. Adaptability: willingness to learn, adapt, and improve from feedback and mentorship\n3. Problem-solving: aptitude for analyzing and solving complex technical problems\n4. Initiative: eagerness to take on new challenges and contribute to the growth of a startup\n\n**Additional Insights:**\n\n* The role offers a chance to actively use the product being built (Sentry's software is used by the team every day)\n* It provides an opportunity to start your career at a high-growth startup\n* You'll be part of a modern software development team that iterates and ships code rapidly\n* You'll have the chance to contribute to an open-source project daily"}
